IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa28-part46`

-- coa28-tests-part46.l4: tests for coa28-part46.l4 (ss 1288-1297). Every expected value was decided by reading the
-- section named beside it, before running; none is copied from the encoding's output.

-- Fixtures: times during which Parliament was dissolved or prorogued, or both Houses were adjourned.
-- columns: first day, last day, kind
`coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025` MEANS `s 1291(2) interval` OF (Date 10 1 2025), (Date 14 1 2025), `s 1291(2) Parliament dissolved or prorogued`
`coa28 test adjourned 10 to 14 January 2025` MEANS `s 1291(2) interval` OF (Date 10 1 2025), (Date 14 1 2025), `s 1291(2) both Houses adjourned`
`coa28 test adjourned 10 to 13 January 2025` MEANS `s 1291(2) interval` OF (Date 10 1 2025), (Date 13 1 2025), `s 1291(2) both Houses adjourned`
`coa28 test adjourned 10 January 2025 only` MEANS `s 1291(2) interval` OF (Date 10 1 2025), (Date 10 1 2025), `s 1291(2) both Houses adjourned`
`coa28 test dissolved 1 to 3 January 2025` MEANS `s 1291(2) interval` OF (Date 1 1 2025), (Date 3 1 2025), `s 1291(2) Parliament dissolved or prorogued`

-- ---- s 1288 (the text: "Except as otherwise provided, regulations and orders under this Act shall be made by statutory instrument")
#ASSERT `s 1288 the regulations or order under this Act must be made by statutory instrument` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1288 the regulations or order under this Act must be made by statutory instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1289 (negative resolution procedure: subject to annulment; every other procedure: a failed "where")
#ASSERT `s 1289 the statutory instrument is subject to annulment in pursuance of a resolution of either House of Parliament` `s 1289 negative resolution procedure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1289 the statutory instrument is subject to annulment in pursuance of a resolution of either House of Parliament` `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1289 the statutory instrument is subject to annulment in pursuance of a resolution of either House of Parliament` `s 1291 approval after being made` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1289 the statutory instrument is subject to annulment in pursuance of a resolution of either House of Parliament` `s 1292(3) no Parliamentary procedure prescribed` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1290 (barred unless the draft has been laid AND approved by each House; only under affirmative procedure)
#ASSERT `s 1290 the regulations or order are barred from being made` `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1290 the regulations or order are barred from being made` `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1290 the regulations or order are barred from being made` `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1290 the regulations or order are barred from being made` `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1290 the regulations or order are barred from being made` `s 1289 negative resolution procedure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1290 the regulations or order are barred from being made` `s 1291 approval after being made` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1291(1)(a) (must be laid before Parliament after being made)
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(a) the requirement to lay the regulations or order before Parliament after being made has been met` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(a) the requirement to lay the regulations or order before Parliament after being made has been met` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1291(2) (no account of time while Parliament is dissolved or prorogued, or both Houses are adjourned for more than four days)
-- Dissolved or prorogued: any length.
#ASSERT `s 1291(2) no account is taken of the time in the interval` `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1291(2) no account is taken of the time in the interval` `coa28 test dissolved 1 to 3 January 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Both Houses adjourned: 10 to 14 January is five days (more than four): disregarded.
#ASSERT `s 1291(2) no account is taken of the time in the interval` `coa28 test adjourned 10 to 14 January 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Both Houses adjourned for four days or fewer: the text says nothing about them (limited by its own wording).
#ASSERT `s 1291(2) no account is taken of the time in the interval` `coa28 test adjourned 10 to 13 January 2025` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1291(2) no account is taken of the time in the interval` `coa28 test adjourned 10 January 2025 only` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Which days fall in a time that is not taken into account (both ends of the interval are inclusive).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` (Date 15 1 2025) EMPTY)
#ASSERT `s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` (Date 10 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`)
#ASSERT `s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` (Date 12 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`)
#ASSERT `s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` (Date 14 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` (Date 9 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` (Date 15 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` (Date 12 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test adjourned 10 to 13 January 2025`))
#ASSERT `s 1291(2) the day falls in a time that is not taken into account` (Date 12 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test adjourned 10 to 14 January 2025`)

-- ---- s 1291(1)(b) (cease to have effect at the end of 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made)
-- Made 1 January 2025: the 28 days are 1 to 28 January.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the last day of the 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made` (Date 1 1 2025) EMPTY EQUALS Date 28 1 2025
-- Made 1 February 2025: 1 to 28 February.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the last day of the 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made` (Date 1 2 2025) EMPTY EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- A dissolution of 10 to 14 January (five days) pushes the end to 2 February.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the last day of the 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made` (Date 1 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`) EQUALS Date 2 2 2025
-- An adjournment of five days counts the same way.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the last day of the 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made` (Date 1 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test adjourned 10 to 14 January 2025`) EQUALS Date 2 2 2025
-- An adjournment of four days is not disregarded: no change.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the last day of the 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made` (Date 1 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test adjourned 10 to 13 January 2025`) EQUALS Date 28 1 2025
-- A dissolution before the day of making does not matter.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the last day of the 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made` (Date 1 2 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
-- A dissolution that covers the first three days: counting starts on 4 January, so day 28 is 31 January.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the last day of the 28 days beginning with the day on which they were made` (Date 1 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 1 to 3 January 2025`) EQUALS Date 31 1 2025
-- Ceasing to have effect, with no approval: still in effect on the 28th day, ceased the day after.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` (Date 1 1 2025) EMPTY (Date 28 1 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` (Date 1 1 2025) EMPTY (Date 29 1 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` (Date 1 1 2025) EMPTY (Date 27 1 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Approved by each House within the period (on the 28th day): they do not cease.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` (Date 1 1 2025) EMPTY (Date 29 1 2025) (JUST (Date 28 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Approved too late (the 29th day): they ceased at the end of the 28th.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` (Date 1 1 2025) EMPTY (Date 30 1 2025) (JUST (Date 29 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- With the five-day dissolution the period runs to 2 February.
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` (Date 1 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`) (Date 2 2 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` (Date 1 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`) (Date 3 2 2025) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1291(1)(b) the regulations or order have ceased to have effect` (Date 1 1 2025) (LIST `coa28 test dissolved 10 to 14 January 2025`) (Date 3 2 2025) (JUST (Date 2 2 2025)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1291(3) (ceasing to have effect does not affect things previously done, or the making of new regulations)
#ASSERT `s 1291(3) the regulations or order ceasing to have effect affects the thing` `s 1291(3)(a) anything previously done under them or it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1291(3) the regulations or order ceasing to have effect affects the thing` `s 1291(3)(b) the making of new regulations or a new order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1291(3) the regulations or order ceasing to have effect affects the thing` `s 1291(3) something else` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1292(2) (regulations and orders interchangeable)
#ASSERT `s 1292(2) the provision may be made by order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1292(2) the provision may be made by order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1292(2) the provision may be made by regulations` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1292(2) the provision may be made by regulations` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1292(3) (no procedure prescribed: negative or affirmative procedure may be used)
#ASSERT `s 1292(3) the provision may be made subject to the procedure` TRUE TRUE `s 1289 negative resolution procedure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1292(3) the provision may be made subject to the procedure` TRUE TRUE `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1292(3) the provision may be made subject to the procedure` TRUE TRUE `s 1291 approval after being made` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1292(3) the provision may be made subject to the procedure` TRUE FALSE `s 1289 negative resolution procedure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1292(3) the provision may be made subject to the procedure` FALSE TRUE `s 1289 negative resolution procedure` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1292(4) (negative procedure provisions may be made under affirmative procedure)
#ASSERT `s 1292(4) the provision may be made subject to affirmative resolution procedure` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1292(4) the provision may be made subject to affirmative resolution procedure` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1292A ("except in section 796, references to the Bank of England do not include the Bank acting as the PRA")
#ASSERT `s 1292A the reference to the Bank of England includes the Bank acting as the Prudential Regulation Authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1292A the reference to the Bank of England includes the Bank acting as the Prudential Regulation Authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1292A the reference to the Bank of England includes the Bank acting as the Prudential Regulation Authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1292A the reference to the Bank of England includes the Bank acting as the Prudential Regulation Authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1293 ("enactment" includes (a), (aa), (b), (c))
#ASSERT `s 1293 the provision is an enactment` `s 1293(a) an enactment contained in subordinate legislation within the meaning of the Interpretation Act 1978` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1293 the provision is an enactment` `s 1293(aa) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, a Measure or Act of the National Assembly for Wales` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1293 the provision is an enactment` `s 1293(b) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1293 the provision is an enactment` `s 1293(c) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, Northern Ireland legislation within the meaning of the Interpretation Act 1978` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1293 the provision is an enactment` `s 1293 another kind of provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1293 the provision is an enactment` `s 1293(b) an enactment contained in, or in an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- ss 1294(6), 1296(4) (the procedure the text attaches to orders)
#ASSERT `s 1294(6) the procedure for an order under section 1294` EQUALS `s 1290 affirmative resolution procedure`
#ASSERT `s 1296(4) the procedure for an order under section 1296` EQUALS `s 1289 negative resolution procedure`

-- ---- s 1297(1) (applies where a provision re-enacts an enactment repealed by this Act)
#ASSERT `s 1297(1) section 1297 applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1297(1) section 1297 applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1297(2) (the repeal and re-enactment does not affect the continuity of the law)
#ASSERT `s 1297(2) the repeal and re-enactment affects the continuity of the law` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1297(2) the repeal and re-enactment affects the continuity of the law` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(2) the repeal and re-enactment affects the continuity of the law` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1297(6) (subject to any specific transitional provision or saving)
#ASSERT `s 1297(6) section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1297(6) section 1297 yields to a specific transitional provision or saving` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1297(3) (things done under the repealed provision have effect as if done under the corresponding provision)
#ASSERT `s 1297(3) the thing has effect thereafter as if done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1297(3) the thing has effect thereafter as if done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(3) the thing has effect thereafter as if done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(3) the thing has effect thereafter as if done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(3) the thing has effect thereafter as if done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1297(3) the thing has effect thereafter as if done under or for the purposes of the corresponding provision of this Act` NOTHING TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1297(4) (references to a provision of this Act include the corresponding repealed provision, so far as the context permits)
#ASSERT `s 1297(4) the reference to the provision of this Act is construed as including a reference to the corresponding repealed provision` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1297(4) the reference to the provision of this Act is construed as including a reference to the corresponding repealed provision` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(4) the reference to the provision of this Act is construed as including a reference to the corresponding repealed provision` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(4) the reference to the provision of this Act is construed as including a reference to the corresponding repealed provision` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(4) the reference to the provision of this Act is construed as including a reference to the corresponding repealed provision` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(4) the reference to the provision of this Act is construed as including a reference to the corresponding repealed provision` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- s 1297(5) (references to a repealed provision include the corresponding provision of this Act)
#ASSERT `s 1297(5) the reference to the repealed provision is construed as being or including a reference to the corresponding provision of this Act` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1297(5) the reference to the repealed provision is construed as being or including a reference to the corresponding provision of this Act` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(5) the reference to the repealed provision is construed as being or including a reference to the corresponding provision of this Act` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(5) the reference to the repealed provision is construed as being or including a reference to the corresponding provision of this Act` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1297(7) (references in this section to this Act include subordinate legislation made under it)
#ASSERT `s 1297(7) the reference to this Act includes the instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1297(7) the reference to this Act includes the instrument` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1297(7) the reference to this Act includes the instrument` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---- s 1297(8) ("subordinate legislation" has the same meaning as in the Interpretation Act 1978: a borrowed answer)
#ASSERT `s 1297(8) the instrument is subordinate legislation for section 1297` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1297(8) the instrument is subordinate legislation for section 1297` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1297(8) the instrument is subordinate legislation for section 1297` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
